A||||2||Adrift||Source for thick wire to use on door locks?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||10-31-2001||11:14 PM||||I snapped/lost some of the "thick wire" which connects from the door lock to the switch - where can I go to buy a similiar thickness wire to bend into place? Whenever I go to home depot and show them the wire they say "What's it from?" I say - "a car" and they say - "Then we won't sell anythign like that here"....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Adrift||10-31-2001||11:19 PM||||something just occured to me - would there be anythign wrong with using a coat hanger for the wire?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-31-2001||11:43 PM||||Coat hanger may work for a while, but will surely flex over time, requiring you to go in there and "rebuild" another one.<P>I imagine that a welding rod would be just right.  Go to your local welder's supply store, and compare what you've got with what they've got.  They come in all sorts of widths and stuff, so you should be able to find something to work.  Welding rod is very sturdy, yet easy enough to form with pliers.  Let us know what you figure out.<P>Oh yeah, if you know of a junkyard with a fiero, just grab one there.  Also, make sure you lube everything good with w-40 or an equivalent oil while in there.  You'll notice everything moves a lot easier <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
